  "interpretation": [
    "Current balanced shared-trace rule has a skew latent-memory constraint in this toy; learned separate Q/K/V and the reader can partially compensate.",
    "General STDP recovers symmetric components but does not exceed Hebbian missing-bit accuracy in the learned experiment.",
    "Independent fixed-activity holdout confirms a conditional benefit for the selected unequal-trace window under persistent shared background.",
    "No observed advantage for that window in the clean condition. This does not establish a domain mismatch or rule out better learned STDP implementations.",
    "In the learned general rule the negative amplitude is larger; the reader can compensate for memory sign. Recovery of a symmetric component is not by itself evidence of selective correction.",
    "The learned programmer was trained on clean storage; noisy cues are tested separately. Its results do not measure learned removal of storage background.",
    "Toy omits positional RoPE and channel-wise trace decay; do not attribute its exact latent skew constraint to the full Sudoku model."
